{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError"],"anchor":"Quantization--Metal-Execution","title":"Quantization & Metal Execution"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Large language models like Llama 3, Mistral, and DeepSeek require massive memory bandwidth. Weight-only quantization (such as GGUF Q4_0 and Q8_0) compresses 16-bit floating-point weights into 4-bit or 8-bit integer blocks with group scaling factors, reducing memory footprint by 50% to 75%.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements native Metal Shading Language (MSL) SIMD kernels executing hardware dequantization and GEMV \/ GEMM transformations directly on Apple Silicon GPUs without intermediate CPU memory allocations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Architecture","anchor":"Architecture","type":"heading"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["Packed Quantized Weights [Q4_0 \/ Q8_0]   Scale Factors [FP16]   Input Activations [FP32]","                 │                               │                        │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────┴────────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                   Metal Compute Command Encoder","                                         │","                 ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐","                 ▼                                               ▼","     MSL Kernel: gemv_q4_0                           MSL Kernel: gemv_q8_0","   - Unpack 4-bit nibbles (w - 8)                  - Load signed 8-bit integers","   - Multiply by group FP16 scale                  - Multiply by group FP16 scale","   - Accumulate with input vector                  - Accumulate with input vector","                 │                                               │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                            Output Activation Vector","                               (Unified Memory)"]},{"level":2,"text":"SIMD-Group Matrix Multiplication","anchor":"SIMD-Group-Matrix-Multiplication","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On Apple Silicon (M-series GPUs), threads within a 32-thread SIMD-group collaborate on 8x8 matrix tiles using ","type":"text"},{"code":"metal_simdgroup_matrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This eliminates thread divergence and ensures maximal utilization of the GPU arithmetic units:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"metal","type":"codeListing","code":["#include <metal_stdlib>","#include <metal_simdgroup_matrix>","","using namespace metal;","","kernel void gemm_simdgroup_q4_0(","    device const half* A               [[buffer(0)]],","    device const half* B               [[buffer(1)]],","    device half* C                     [[buffer(2)]],","    constant uint& M                   [[buffer(3)]],","    constant uint& N                   [[buffer(4)]],","    constant uint& K                   [[buffer(5)]],","    uint2 threadgroup_position_in_grid [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]],","    uint simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]",") {","    simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8> acc;","    acc = make_filled_simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8>(0.0h);","    \/\/ Accumulate across inner K dimension...","}"]},{"level":2,"text":"Swift API Integration","anchor":"Swift-API-Integration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"QuantizedLinear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exposes both MLX tensor inference and direct Metal kernel execution:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftLLM","","\/\/ 1. Create a quantized linear layer (e.g. 4096 in, 4096 out)","let linear = QuantizedLinear(","    inFeatures: 4096,","    outFeatures: 4096,","    scheme: .q4_0,","    weight: mlxWeights,","    scales: mlxScales",")","","\/\/ 2. Direct Metal shader execution without CPU round-trips","let outputs = try linear.forwardMetal(","    inVector: inputActivations,","    rawWeights: packedQ4Bytes,","    rawScales: fp16Scales",")"]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Hardware dequantization and SIMD-group matrix multiplication for 4-bit and 8-bit quantized weights on Apple Silicon GPU.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalshadersquantization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization"},"metadata":{"title":"Native Metal MSL Shaders for Quantized LLMs","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials"}],"references":{"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizedLinear":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizedLinear"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizedlinear","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizedLinear"}],"title":"QuantizedLinear","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A linear neural network layer performing matrix multiplication with 4-bit (Q4_0, Q4_K) or 8-bit quantized weights."}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/WeightParsingAndSampling":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/weightparsingandsampling","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Parse GGUF and SafeTensors model weights zero-copy and sample tokens using Temperature and Top-K sampling.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"GGUF\/SafeTensors Parsing & Sampling"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM":{"title":"SwiftLLM","abstract":[{"text":"Local Causal Transformer Decoder & Weight Parsers.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/MetalQuantizedEngine":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalquantizedengine","title":"MetalQuantizedEngine","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thread-safe executor and pipeline cache for Metal quantized MSL GEMV \/ GEMM kernels."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MetalQuantizedEngine","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MetalQuantizedEngine","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizationScheme":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"QuantizationScheme","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizationscheme","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"QuantizationScheme","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"QuantizationScheme","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The quantization scheme used for compressed model weights."}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/